<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>German economy returns to growth, so why is the country still worried?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:753069836c81a9efc387cadbe7e3509026c3ad1b51a6525b5fb9d8f22eda3aa8</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220--24d2aa1d0aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German economy is growing again, albeit slightly. However, economists warn that without reforms, higher productivity and solid public finances, a loss of prosperity and growing debt threaten future generations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How AI is likely to change Germany's job market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fc518809769164d64c7a4a59bfc2b8a3e444aa5e9d395637ae9240802eb50b4</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597--3a5b2bd9406d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. But economists aren't convinced, and campaigners think we need to ask deeper questions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's 2027 budget: A record €561 billion and a mountain of debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e8785ffa12c4d0bd46e5633e84612d0026ed37abf4078760d9555d14246266e</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-_561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216--747b01c10ad0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-€561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2027 federal budget proposal has finally been hammered out and is set for a vote in parliament. What are the government's policy priorities in defense, infrastructure, the economy and social spending?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Holzer Prize awarded to Katja Gloger and DW's Jaafar Abdul Karim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71f2bae0a9a38a05302e477820fc6ca6ce5111a1af9fd7d4b51ca26e3eb823b8</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916--5a434ad9f59c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW journalist Jaafar Abdul Karim and Russia correspondent Katja Gloger have been awarded the prestigious Werner Holzer Prize for international journalism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Wolf Biermann at 90: The singer who defied East Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61beefc4779f2eaf31276b325e7dcc53464a736bb36943d3dcd3c88088ffe898</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297--17726feda083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">His life is a reflection of contemporary German history, which Biermann has addressed via his songs and sharp wit. Turning 90, he’s as feisty as ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
